      "fullContent": "X 上的 Rohan Paul：“Verified AI just had its greatest month.\nA swarm of AI agents just did what no mathematician could do alone: check every step of the longest proof in history.\nFor 40+ years, mathematicians have built on the Classification of Finite Simple Groups without anyone being able to check… / X\n发帖\n登录 注册\n发帖\n登录 注册\nX 上的 Rohan Paul：“Verified AI just had its greatest month.\nA swarm of AI agents just did what no mathematician could do alone: check every step of the longest proof in history.\nFor 40+ years, mathematicians have built on the Classification of Finite Simple Groups without anyone being able to check it alone.\nAxiom’s AI agent swarm just did it in 24 days, turned 15,000 pages across 500+ papers into 38M+ lines of machine-verified code. And it also uncovered 34 serious discrepancies in the published record.”\nRohan Paul\n@rohanpaul_ai\n显示翻译\nVerified AI just had its greatest month.\nA swarm of AI agents just did what no mathematician could do alone: check every step of the longest proof in history.\nFor 40+ years, mathematicians have built on the Classification of Finite Simple Groups without anyone being able to check it alone.\nAxiom’s AI agent swarm just did it in 24 days, turned 15,000 pages across 500+ papers into 38M+ lines of machine-verified code. And it also uncovered 34 serious discrepancies in the published record.\nLeo\n@biosemiote\n7小时\nThe formal proof of CFSG may now be among the largest open-source projects ever. Watching agents assemble it is a reminder of the awe-inspiring human achievement behind it. The graph represents some 15,000 pages of intricate arguments developed by mathematicians over decades.\n00:00\n付费合作\n23:31 · 2026年10月27日 · 3,627\n浏览量\n14\n5\n24\n5\nRohan Paul\n@rohanpaul_ai\n显示翻译\nVerified AI just had its greatest month.\nA swarm of AI agents just did what no mathematician could do alone: check every step of the longest proof in history.\nFor 40+ years, mathematicians have built on the Classification of Finite Simple Groups without anyone being able to check it alone.\nAxiom’s AI agent swarm just did it in 24 days, turned 15,000 pages across 500+ papers into 38M+ lines of machine-verified code. And it also uncovered 34 serious discrepancies in the published record.\nLeo\n@biosemiote\n7小时\nThe formal proof of CFSG may now be among the largest open-source projects ever. Watching agents assemble it is a reminder of the awe-inspiring human achievement behind it. The graph represents some 15,000 pages of intricate arguments developed by mathematicians over decades.\n00:00\n付费合作\n23:31 · 2026年10月27日 · 3,627\n浏览量\n14\n5\n24\n5\nRohan Paul\n@rohanpaul_ai\n7小时\nTheir official technical report\naxiommath.ai\nFormalizing the Enormous Theorem\nAxiom has formalized in Lean the classification of finite simple groups, the longest proof in the history of mathematics.\n1\n1\n697\nRivers\n@JohnnyRivers33\n6小时\nLean verification is flawed. I’ve already told you this. Now you are engaging in purposeful misinformation because you are a sycophantic sociopath that can’t admit you are causing a massive disaster and mess. I’m filing a lawsuit against axiom and every other ai company doing 显示更多\n1\n16"
