      "fullContent": "X 上的 Rohan Paul：“Meta filed the announcement with the SEC that it plans to raise $95B in new equity to fund AI data centers and its superintelligence push.\nThe first $35B comes from underwritten offerings of $22.5B in common stock and $12.5B in mandatory convertible preferred shares, with a $60B a… / X\n发帖\n登录 注册\n发帖\n登录 注册\nX 上的 Rohan Paul：“Meta filed the announcement with the SEC that it plans to raise $95B in new equity to fund AI data centers and its superintelligence push.\nThe first $35B comes from underwritten offerings of $22.5B in common stock and $12.5B in mandatory convertible preferred shares, with a $60B at-the-market program to follow.\nNvidia, AMD and Broadcom, which sell Meta the chips this money will buy, indicated interest in taking up to $5B of the shares.\nThe raise comes as Meta’s 2026 capex forecast rose to $135B to $145B while free cash flow turned negative, despite $97B of operating cash flow in the first 3 quarters and about $82B in cash and securities.\nMeta says the money supports 4 superclusters above 1 gigawatt each, its Muse agent and a data center business, alongside debt and partnership financing.”\nRohan Paul\n@rohanpaul_ai\n显示翻译\nMeta filed the announcement with the SEC that it plans to raise $95B in new equity to fund AI data centers and its superintelligence push.\nThe first $35B comes from underwritten offerings of $22.5B in common stock and $12.5B in mandatory convertible preferred shares, with a $60B at-the-market program to follow.\nNvidia, AMD and Broadcom, which sell Meta the chips this money will buy, indicated interest in taking up to $5B of the shares.\nThe raise comes as Meta’s 2026 capex forecast rose to $135B to $145B while free cash flow turned negative, despite $97B of operating cash flow in the first 3 quarters and about $82B in cash and securities.\nMeta says the money supports 4 superclusters above 1 gigawatt each, its Muse agent and a data center business, alongside debt and partnership financing.\n18:40 · 2026年10月26日 · 5,421\n浏览量\n14\n7\n21\n3\nRohan Paul\n@rohanpaul_ai\n显示翻译\nMeta filed the announcement with the SEC that it plans to raise $95B in new equity to fund AI data centers and its superintelligence push.\nThe first $35B comes from underwritten offerings of $22.5B in common stock and $12.5B in mandatory convertible preferred shares, with a $60B at-the-market program to follow.\nNvidia, AMD and Broadcom, which sell Meta the chips this money will buy, indicated interest in taking up to $5B of the shares.\nThe raise comes as Meta’s 2026 capex forecast rose to $135B to $145B while free cash flow turned negative, despite $97B of operating cash flow in the first 3 quarters and about $82B in cash and securities.\nMeta says the money supports 4 superclusters above 1 gigawatt each, its Muse agent and a data center business, alongside debt and partnership financing.\n18:40 · 2026年10月26日 · 5,421\n浏览量\n14\n7\n21\n3\nRohan Paul\n@rohanpaul_ai\n10月26日\nsec.gov/Archives/edgar…\n2\n784"
