    {
      "id": "ub3gw75dlj8fpfm63er4k1xn2",
      "title": "Artificial Analysis 评测 GPT-6.1 Terra：以不到三分之一成本推进性价比前沿",
      "title_en": "GPT-6.1 Terra pushes the cost efficiency frontier",
      "url": "https://artificialanalysis.ai/articles/gpt-6-1-terra-pushes-the-cost-efficiency-frontier",
      "permalink": "https://aihot.news/items/ub3gw75dlj8fpfm63er4k1xn2",
      "source": "Artificial Analysis 完整文章（网页）",
      "publishedAt": "2026-10-25T16:00:00.000Z",
      "discoveredAt": "2026-10-26T18:33:19.250Z",
      "summary": "Artificial Analysis 评测 OpenAI 发布的 GPT-6.1 Terra，称其在低中 effort 下达到智能与成本的 Pareto 前沿，价格为 GPT-5.6 Terra 的一半或更低（$1/$5 每百万输入/输出 token）。",
      "category": "c4",
      "score": 76,
      "selected": true,
      "attribution": {
        "source": "AIHOT",
        "canonical": "https://aihot.news/items/ub3gw75dlj8fpfm63er4k1xn2"
      },
      "tag": "AI动态",
      "tagClass": "tag-neutral",
      "fullContent": "GPT-6.1 Terra pushes the cost efficiency frontier | Artificial Analysis\nArtificial Analysis K\nAll articles\nOctober 26, 2026\nOpenAI has released GPT-6.1 Terra, pushing the cost efficiency frontier. It is the first Terra-class model since GPT-5.6, and is more intelligent for less than a third of the cost\nSee model page\nPricing per token is half or less that of GPT-5.6 Terra - at $1/$5 per million input/output tokens vs $2/$12 for the previous model. Cache write has also halved, now at $1.25 per million tokens. Cached input is one quarter at $0.05 vs $0.20 per million tokens.\nKey takeaways:\n➤ Pareto-optimal for Intelligence vs Cost at low and medium effort: At max effort, GPT-6.1 Terra gains 6 points in the Artificial Analysis Intelligence Index over GPT-5.6 Terra, at less than a third of the cost per task ($0.40 vs $1.40). At lower effort levels the gain is larger, between 7 and 13 points. The low and medium effort levels are Pareto-optimal for cost efficiency, while the other effort levels sit behind the frontier. At max effort, the model scores 4 points below GPT-6.1 Sol and 10 points above GPT-6 Luna in the Intelligence Index.\n➤ Pushes the Coding Agent Index cost efficiency frontier: With a score of 48 in the newly released Artificial Analysis Coding Agent Index v2.0, the model is 6 points below GPT-6.1 Sol (54) and 17 points above GPT-6 Luna (31). The xhigh and low effort settings sit on the frontier of cost efficiency in the Coding Agent Index, while other effort levels are behind the frontier.\n➤ 50 point drop in hallucination rate: GPT-6.1 Terra guesses 38% of the time when it does not know the answer to a question in AA-Omniscience, our private knowledge and hallucination benchmark. Previously, GPT-5.6 Terra's hallucination rate was 88%. This significant reduction in hallucination is coupled with a 2 point increase in AA-Omniscience accuracy - meaning the model simultaneously answers more questions correctly.\n➤ 20 point jump in Terminal-Bench 4.0, small improvements across most evaluations: The model makes significant progress in the terminal-based agentic benchmark, Terminal-Bench 4.0, with a gain of ~20 points, now rivaling GPT-6.1 Sol at max effort. Gains across most other evaluations are smaller, for example, 5 points in GDP.pdf.\nWith a score of 48 in the Artificial Analysis Coding Agent Index v2.0, GPT-6.1 Terra is 6 points below GPT-6.1 Sol (54) and 17 points above GPT-6 Luna (31). The xhigh and low effort settings sit on the frontier of cost efficiency.\nGPT-6.1 Terra shows a 50 point drop in hallucination rate, measured in AA-Omniscience. This is coupled with a 2 point increase in AA-Omniscience accuracy - meaning the model simultaneously answers more questions correctly.\nThe model makes significant progress in the terminal-based agentic benchmark, Terminal-Bench 4.0, with a gain of ~20 points, now rivaling GPT-6.1 Sol at max effort.\nBreakdown of the individual evaluations in the Artificial Analysis Intelligence Index v4.3.2\nCompare GPT-6.1 Terra with other leading models at: https://artificialanalysis.ai/models/releases/gpt-6-1-terra\nRead the latest\nAnnouncing Artificial Analysis Intelligence Index v5\nIndex v5 features 2 new benchmarks and 3 upgrades. For the first time, the majority of the Index is built on private datasets\nOctober 27, 2026\nCode2Video-AA: how well do AI models design videos in code?\nArtificial Analysis' implementation of HeyGen's Code2Video Bench, evaluating how well models create short product and brand videos from 114 design briefs using HyperFrames HTML.\nOctober 26, 2026\nKimi K3.1 Pro launches at 4th on the Intelligence Index and will lead open weights models\nKimi K3.1 Pro launches at 4th on the Artificial Analysis Intelligence Index and will lead open weights models\nOctober 23, 2026\nArtificial Analysis\nExplore\nLLM Leaderboard\nImage Arena\nVideo Arena\nAI Agents\nEvaluations\nProducts\nOptima\nMicroEvals\nModel Recommender\nData Playground\nImage Lab\nCompany\nAbout\nMethodology\nContact\nArticles\nCareers\nX LinkedIn YouTube Rednote Discord\n© 2026 Artificial Analysis\nTerms of Use Data Platform Terms Privacy Policy English"
