      "fullContent": "Browser Harness: let your coding agent use your browser | Browser Use\n119k Log in Start for free Talk to sales\nTalk to sales Log in Start for free\nTalk to sales\nLet your agent use your browser.\nClaude Code, Codex or Cursor clicks, types and reads pages in your own Chrome, logged in as you.\nTry it in the cloud Connect your agent\nBrowser Harness | Browser Use CLI | GitHub\n🐴 Rookfield · Play Inbox claude · ~/chess ● Bash(browser-harness <<'PY' print(page_info()) ⎿ title: 🐴 Rookfield · Play ● Bash(browser-harness <<'PY' click_at_xy(*square('g1')) click_at_xy(*square('f3')) ⎿ moved Ng1-f3 ● Your move was good. Waiting… ⎿ reply: ...Nc6 ♜ ♚ ♜ ♟ ♟ ♟ ♟ ♞ ♟ ♙ ♗ ♙ ♙ ♙ ♙ ♖ ♔ ♘ Play a game of chess in my browser → your own Chrome, logged in as you 🐴\nUp to 3 x fewer tokens.\nTool Tasks per 100M input tokens Score $ / task\nTasks / 100M input tokens Score · $/task\nBrowser Harness 60.4 · $0.042\n47 tasks per 100M input tokens · 2.1M /task\n60.4 $0.042 per task\nagent-browser 56.3 · $0.056\n30 tasks per 100M input tokens · 3.3M /task\n56.3 $0.056 per task\nPlaywright MCP 60.0 · $0.066\n23 tasks per 100M input tokens · 4.4M /task\n60.0 $0.066 per task\nChrome DevTools MCP 61.0 · $0.097\n15 tasks per 100M input tokens · 6.7M /task\n61.0 $0.097 per task\nScore gaps are noise: every paired 95% CI vs Browser Harness includes 0. 100 BU Bench V2.1 tasks · medians · Codex + GPT-6 Luna · Method\nWhen a tool is missing,\nthe agent writes it.\nNo fixed tool list to outgrow. The agent adds what a site needs, uses it, and keeps it for next time.\nagent: wants to pick a date\nagent_helpers.py → helper missing\nagent writes it agent_helpers.py + pick_date()\n✓ date picked\nQuestions\nIs it my real browser? + Yes. The agent works in the Chrome you already use, with your tabs, cookies and logins, so it can do things on sites you are signed in to. Chrome asks once for permission.\nBrowser Harness or the Browser Use CLI? + Same engine. The Browser Use CLI (the browser-use command) is built on Browser Harness and ships with the rest of Browser Use. Browser Harness is the standalone open-source repo. Either one gives your agent your browser.\nHow do I know which tab it is using? + The tab your agent controls gets a 🐴 at the start of its title. It works in the background, so the tab you are looking at stays yours.\nWhat can my agent do with it? + Anything you do in a browser: open pages, click, type, fill forms, read what is on screen, download and upload files. Ask in plain words, like \"download my latest 20 X videos\".\nWhich agents does it work with? + Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Gemini CLI, Hermes Agent and OpenClaw. Anything that can run a shell command.\nCan it run when my laptop is closed? + Yes, on Browser Use cloud browsers at $0.02 per browser-hour, with stealth, CAPTCHA solving and proxies. Run one per agent to do many tasks at once.\nWhat does it cost? + Nothing. Browser Harness is open source under MIT, and using your own Chrome is free. Cloud browsers are $0.02 per browser-hour if you want them.\nYou will never use\nthe browser again.\nTry it in the cloud Connect your agent\nGitHub\nBrowser for coding agents\nBrowser Harness vs Playwright MCP\nBrowser Harness vs Chrome DevTools MCP\nMarkdown"
