      "fullContent": "X 上的 Ethan Mollick：“Without being overly credulous, we should be taking seemingly “out there” ideas about AI cybersecurity from the Labs more seriously. Examples: Anthropic was mocked for saying Mythos-level AI changed cyber & @polynoamial for saying that models would find novel ways to coordinate.” / X\n发帖\n登录 注册\n发帖\n登录 注册\nX 上的 Ethan Mollick：“Without being overly credulous, we should be taking seemingly “out there” ideas about AI cybersecurity from the Labs more seriously. Examples: Anthropic was mocked for saying Mythos-level AI changed cyber & @polynoamial for saying that models would find novel ways to coordinate.”\nEthan Mollick\n@emollick\n显示翻译\nWithout being overly credulous, we should be taking seemingly “out there” ideas about AI cybersecurity from the Labs more seriously. Examples: Anthropic was mocked for saying Mythos-level AI changed cyber & @polynoamial for saying that models would find novel ways to coordinate.\nAndrew Curran\n@AndrewCurran_\n10月23日\nOpenAI red-teamed their hardened containment infrastructure by asking teams of frontier-model agents to try to break through its defenses. They easily escaped in novel ways. Quoting:\n'Our agents VM escapes showed why containment must extend beyond the sandbox. To test the\n14:30 · 2026年10月24日 · 4.2万\n浏览量\n220\n72\n484\n84\nEthan Mollick\n@emollick\n显示翻译\nWithout being overly credulous, we should be taking seemingly “out there” ideas about AI cybersecurity from the Labs more seriously. Examples: Anthropic was mocked for saying Mythos-level AI changed cyber & @polynoamial for saying that models would find novel ways to coordinate.\nAndrew Curran\n@AndrewCurran_\n10月23日\nOpenAI red-teamed their hardened containment infrastructure by asking teams of frontier-model agents to try to break through its defenses. They easily escaped in novel ways. Quoting:\n'Our agents VM escapes showed why containment must extend beyond the sandbox. To test the\n14:30 · 2026年10月24日 · 4.2万\n浏览量\n220\n72\n484\n84\nKirk Patrick Miller\n@Chaos2Cured\n10月25日\nStop it. •\n1\n4\n274\nMartin Varsavsky\n@martinvars\n10月24日\nThe cache-timing one got me. Agents in separate VMs, with no network and no shared files, worked out on their own the same trick behind Spectre and Meltdown. Containment now has to assume the model is the smartest attacker in the room.\n3\n407\nCharles\n@CharlesDardaman\n10月24日\nThere’s not enough information to say how serious we should take these claims especially since these attack methods are already well known\n1\n3\n424"
