      "fullContent": "OpenAI lowers valuation target, raises up to $30 billion Ad\nSkip to content\nSign In\nRegister\nSubscribe Now The Decoder\nOpens discord in a new tab Opens LinkedIn in a new tab\nOpenAI lowers valuation target, raises up to $30 billion\nMaximilian Schreiner View the LinkedIn Profile of Maximilian Schreiner\nOct 23, 2026\nOpenAI is closing in on a new funding round of up to $30 billion but has lowered its valuation target to get there. The company originally pitched investors on a $1.4 trillion valuation, according to internal documents obtained by the Financial Times . That number has since dropped to $1.25 trillion, CNBC also reports . The FT says demand was weaker than in previous rounds, with some backers experiencing \"indigestion\" after heavy investments in earlier fundraises.\nUAE investors and investment firm Coatue are leading the $30 billion round. The funding is being positioned as a bridge ahead of a potential IPO. OpenAI is also negotiating a commercial deal to secure additional compute capacity through the UAE, according to CNBC.\nOpenAI confidentially filed an IPO prospectus with the SEC in June. CFO Sarah Friar told employees in August that OpenAI would be a publicly traded company by 2027. CEO Sam Altman said in September that the timing was unfavorable for going public . He had already communicated that internally back in June. Competitor Anthropic is also preparing an IPO and is targeting a valuation between $1.5 and $2 trillion. Ad\nAd\nAI News Without the Hype – Curated by Humans\nSubscribe to THE DECODER for ad-free reading, a weekly AI newsletter, our exclusive \"AI Radar\" frontier report six times a year, full archive access, and access to our comment section.\nSubscribe now\nSource: CNBC\nMost Popular\nStanford and Arc Institute scientists used AI to design new viruses that killed bacteria in the lab\nFrontier Radar #4: China has caught up, so what's left of the Western AI lead?\nStudy explains why AI agents benefit from \"skills\" and when they fail\nAI keeps cracking unsolved math problems, and mathematicians have mixed feelings\nAnthropic wants you to know Claude leads a quarter of its research, but \"lead\" doesn't mean what you think\nMeta's new frontier model Muse Wonder Full breaks into the AI top tier\nAI Community & Insights\nThe Decoder\nFollow The Decoder for AI news, background stories and expert analyses.\nOpens LinkedIn in a new tab Opens Discord in a new tab\nAd\nBETA-TEST\n×\nwpDiscuz\nInsert\nOpens discord in a new tab Opens discord in a new tab\nInformation\nAbout\nAdvertise\nPublish with us\nLogin\nTopics\nAI and society\nAI in practice\nAI research\nFrontier Radar\nShort News\nLegal\nPrivacy Policy\nPrivacy Manager\nImprint\nTerms and Conditions\nCancellation & Refund\nTHE DECODER by DEEP CONTENT by heise | All rights reserved 2026\nBETA-TEST\n×\nwpDiscuz\nInsert"
