      "fullContent": "X 上的 Rohan Paul：“WSJ: OpenAI fired 3 safety researchers after security staff found disappearing Signal chats with an outside safety researcher.\nThe phone checks started after a September news report said OpenAI’s newest model, Astra, uses a new method that makes it smarter but writes down less of… / X\n发帖\n登录 注册\n发帖\n登录 注册\nX 上的 Rohan Paul：“WSJ: OpenAI fired 3 safety researchers after security staff found disappearing Signal chats with an outside safety researcher.\nThe phone checks started after a September news report said OpenAI’s newest model, Astra, uses a new method that makes it smarter but writes down less of its thinking, so humans can see less of how it reaches answers.\nso the concern was, if future models think without writing those steps down, as the researchers feared Astra-style designs might, investigators would see only what the agents did, not why.\nOpenAI treated that report as a leak of its secret model design and began hunting for the source.\nInvestigators named Ryan Greenblatt, who helped METR analyse logs from July’s Hugging Face hack, as the suspected leaker; he denies it.”\nRohan Paul\n@rohanpaul_ai\n显示翻译\nWSJ: OpenAI fired 3 safety researchers after security staff found disappearing Signal chats with an outside safety researcher.\nThe phone checks started after a September news report said OpenAI’s newest model, Astra, uses a new method that makes it smarter but writes down less of its thinking, so humans can see less of how it reaches answers.\nso the concern was, if future models think without writing those steps down, as the researchers feared Astra-style designs might, investigators would see only what the agents did, not why.\nOpenAI treated that report as a leak of its secret model design and began hunting for the source.\nInvestigators named Ryan Greenblatt, who helped METR analyse logs from July’s Hugging Face hack, as the suspected leaker; he denies it.\n6:04 · 2026年10月23日 · 1.3万\n浏览量\n15\n14\n112\n31\nRohan