      "fullContent": "X 上的 Rohan Paul：“WSJ: Musk wants to combine a $2T rocket company with a $1.5T carmaker around AI.\nSpaceX’s AI unit is now its largest business, with third-quarter revenue of $7.56B against $813M a year earlier, and more than $16.4B of its $19.6B quarterly capital spending went to AI.\nThat growth… / X\n发帖\n登录 注册\n发帖\n登录 注册\nX 上的 Rohan Paul：“WSJ: Musk wants to combine a $2T rocket company with a $1.5T carmaker around AI.\nSpaceX’s AI unit is now its largest business, with third-quarter revenue of $7.56B against $813M a year earlier, and more than $16.4B of its $19.6B quarterly capital spending went to AI.\nThat growth turned SpaceX to a $4.4B quarterly profit from a $1.05B loss, giving it the financial weight to absorb Tesla rather than the reverse.\nThe AI case for the merger treats Tesla’s robotaxis and Optimus robots as the front end and SpaceX’s data centers and satellite links as the infrastructure they would depend on.”\nRohan Paul\n@rohanpaul_ai\n显示翻译\nWSJ: Musk wants to combine a $2T rocket company with a $1.5T carmaker around AI.\nSpaceX’s AI unit is now its largest business, with third-quarter revenue of $7.56B against $813M a year earlier, and more than $16.4B of its $19.6B quarterly capital spending went to AI.\nThat growth turned SpaceX to a $4.4B quarterly profit from a $1.05B loss, giving it the financial weight to absorb Tesla rather than the reverse.\nThe AI case for the merger treats Tesla’s robotaxis and Optimus robots as the front end and SpaceX’s data centers and satellite links as the infrastructure they would depend on.\n3:16 · 2026年10月22日 · 8,036\n浏览量\n11\n9\n66\n12\nRohan Paul\n@rohanpaul_ai\n显示翻译\nWSJ: Musk wants to combine a $2T rocket company with a $1.5T carmaker around AI.\nSpaceX’s AI unit is now its largest business, with third-quarter revenue of $7.56B against $813M a year earlier, and more than $16.4B of its $19.6B quarterly capital spending went to AI.\nThat growth turned SpaceX to a $4.4B quarterly profit from a $1.05B loss, giving it the financial weight to absorb Tesla rather than the reverse.\nThe AI case for the merger treats Tesla’s robotaxis and Optimus robots as the front end and SpaceX’s data centers and satellite links as the infrastructure they would depend on.\n3:16 · 2026年10月22日 · 8,036\n浏览量\n11\n9\n66\n12\nRohan Paul\n@rohanpaul_ai\n10月22日\nSpaceX and Tesla Are Already Joined at the Hip. What a Formal Merger Would Mean.\n自 wsj.com\n2\n965\nChahat Sharma\n@Chahatusharma\n10月22日\nso 16.4B of AI capex in one quarter vs 7.56B of AI revenue, more than double what it brought in. is the 4.4B profit after that spend or is most of it sitting on the balance sheet to depreciate later?\n91"
