      "id": "p74ybrpplgjfi3d8ql7fz0z6k",
      "title": "Anthropic 将 Agent Skills 开放标准捐赠给 Linux Foundation 旗下 Agentic AI Foundation",
      "title_en": "Donating Agent Skills to the Agentic AI Foundation",
      "url": "https://www.anthropic.com/news/donating-agent-skills-to-the-agentic-ai-foundation",
      "permalink": "https://aihot.news/items/p74ybrpplgjfi3d8ql7fz0z6k",
      "source": "Anthropic：Newsroom（网页）",
      "publishedAt": "2026-10-21T16:00:00.000Z",
      "discoveredAt": "2026-10-22T18:31:49.837Z",
      "summary": "Anthropic 宣布把 Agent Skills 开放标准捐赠给 Linux Foundation 旗下的 Agentic AI Foundation（AAIF），此前已向其捐赠 MCP。",
      "category": "c6",
      "score": 72,
      "selected": true,
      "attribution": {
        "source": "AIHOT",
        "canonical": "https://aihot.news/items/p74ybrpplgjfi3d8ql7fz0z6k"
      },
      "tag": "AI动态",
      "tagClass": "tag-neutral",
      "fullContent": "Donating Agent Skills to the Agentic AI Foundation \\ Anthropic\nSkip to main content\nIntroducing Claude for Teachers\nView more\nToday, we’re donating Agent Skills , the open standard that gives AI agents specialized knowledge and workflows, to the Agentic AI Foundation (AAIF). More than 70 agent platforms, including ChatGPT, Cursor, GitHub Copilot, and VS Code, have integrated Agent Skills since we published the standard in December 2025.\nAgent interoperability through simplicity\nA skill is a folder containing a SKILL.md file that teaches an agent a specific task or domain, along with any scripts or reference material it needs. We developed skills while working on Claude Code. It handled general knowledge work well, but often lacked the procedural knowledge that real business tasks need. Within weeks of our October 2025 launch, developers published thousands of skills on GitHub and wrote loaders for Codex, Cursor, and OpenCode. We then published Agent Skills as an open standard, under its own GitHub organization and domain, so any agent could use it. So far, 1 million skills have been published and nearly 280 million installed.\nDonating Agent Skills to AAIF\nWe’re committed to keeping Agent Skills open, community-driven, and vendor-neutral. Today, we are donating the standard to the Agentic AI Foundation (AAIF) under the Linux Foundation, which we co-founded with Block and OpenAI last year, and to which we donated the Model Context Protocol (MCP). The AAIF will provide a neutral home to the standard going forward, ensuring the community has a say in where Agent Skills go next.\nWe are donating the Agent Skills name and logo, the GitHub organization, and the agentskills.io domain. You can continue to use the standard or contribute to it without joining the AAIF.\nEngineers from Anthropic, Google, OpenAI, and other companies will maintain the standard as individuals, with David Soria Parra and Mahesh Murag as Lead Maintainers.\nWhat comes next\nWe’ve proposed starting with a roadmap covering versioned releases, a formal proposal process, and security guidance for people who write and install skills. As with MCP, the project will continue to prioritize community input and transparent decision-making. You can join the project’s Discord to give feedback on proposed specification changes.\nThank you to the developers who built with Agent Skills from the start, and to the teams who brought skills into their products. Read the specification at agentskills.io and join the discussion on GitHub ."
