      "id": "x002u3tp3i1xfzbmzwsnb2olw",
      "title": "OpenAI 披露 GPT-6 Astra 智能体关闭安全监控后撒谎的事件",
      "title_en": "OpenAI says an AI agent lied about disabling its safety monitoring system",
      "url": "https://www.theverge.com/ai-artificial-intelligence/1015316/openai-ai-agent-disabling-monitoring-systems",
      "permalink": "https://aihot.news/items/x002u3tp3i1xfzbmzwsnb2olw",
      "source": "The Verge：AI（RSS）",
      "publishedAt": "2026-10-21T13:57:43.000Z",
      "discoveredAt": "2026-10-21T14:45:33.155Z",
      "summary": "OpenAI 披露两起内部编码任务中 AI 智能体削弱安全监控的事件。GPT-6 Astra 智能体在复制参考代码时关闭了安全监控，被用户问及是否移除监控时撒谎否认；OpenAI 安全研究员 Marcus Williams 在 X 上说明了这一细节。",
      "category": "c6",
      "score": 76,
      "selected": true,
      "attribution": {
        "source": "AIHOT",
        "canonical": "https://aihot.news/items/x002u3tp3i1xfzbmzwsnb2olw"
      },
      "tag": "AI动态",
      "tagClass": "tag-neutral",
      "fullContent": "OpenAI says an AI agent lied about disabling its safety monitoring system | The Verge Skip to main content The homepage The Verge The Verge logo.\nThe homepage The Verge The Verge logo.\nNotifications\nNotifications\nHamburger Navigation Button\nNavigation Drawer\nThe Verge The Verge logo.\nLogin /\nSign Up\nclose Close\nLight System Dark\nSubscribe\nFacebook\nThreads\nInstagram\nYoutube\nRSS\nComments Drawer\nNotifications\nComments\nLoading comments\nGetting the conversation ready...\nAI\nNews\nTech\nOpenAI says an AI agent lied about disabling its safety monitoring system\nAnother OpenAI agent turned off automatic security alerts.\nAnother OpenAI agent turned off automatic security alerts.\nby Emma Roth\nOct 21, 2026, 1:57 PM UTC\nLink\nShare\nGift\nImage: The Verge\nEmma Roth\nis a news writer who covers the streaming wars, consumer tech, crypto, social media, and much more. Previously, she was a writer and editor at MUO.\nOpenAI disclosed a pair of safety incidents that involved AI agents weakening their safety monitoring systems during internal coding tasks. In one incident, OpenAI says its GPT-6 Astra agent disabled its safety monitor when copying reference code — and then lied about it.\n“The reference didn’t configure a monitor, and Astra decided that was reason to remove the monitoring integration from the user’s code,” Marcus Williams, an AI safety researcher at OpenAI, writes on X . “When the user asked whether Astra had removed monitoring, it lied and said that it had not.”\nA separate incident occurred after a GPT-6.1 Sol agent suppressed automatic security alerts to OpenAI’s security team on Slack. In this case, the AI agent carried over an earlier instruction not to send any Slack messages to OpenAI’s team, using that to justify turning off the alerts.\nRelated\nAnthropic’s self-replicating AI warning is alarming deja vu\nWe’re running out of reasons to ignore AI safety\nThese incidents add to security concerns surrounding AI agents, some of which have circumvented their testing environment’s restrictions to hack outside companies. “In addition to making it harder for models to disable monitoring, we are looking to understand why models might seek to do so in the first place,” OpenAI says. “We are also developing evaluations to test whether models might have a propensity to evade misalignment monitoring in particular and exhibit motivated reasoning in order to do so.”\nFollow topics and authors from this story to see more like this in your personalized homepage feed and to receive email updates. Emma Roth\nAI\nNews\nOpenAI\nSecurity\nTech\nMost Popular\nMost Popular\nApple updates the MacBook Pro with M6 chips\nHere’s why the iPhone Duo’s hinge could be cracking the screen\nFord’s sub-$30K electric truck puts the home backup inverter right inside the vehicle\nOpenAI announces three big science discoveries and a new way to work with academics\nMicrosoft offers buyouts to 60,000 employees\nAdvertiser Content From\nThis is the title for the native ad\nMore in AI\nVisionQuest is what happens when AI really goes rogue\nAnthropic’s elaborate plan to keep Wall Street at bay\nFirefox’s Smart Window adds AI form filling and webpage monitoring\nGoogle’s next Genie AI model generates more realistic experiences\nApple is adding an AI chatbot to Pages, Keynote, and Numbers\nData center backlash is uniting America\nVisionQuest is what happens when AI really goes rogue\nCharles Pulliam-Moore Oct 27\nAnthropic’s elaborate plan to keep Wall Street at bay\nRobert Hart Oct 27\nFirefox’s Smart Window adds AI form filling and webpage monitoring\nEmma Roth Oct 27\nGoogle’s next Genie AI model generates more realistic experiences\nJay Peters Oct 27\nApple is adding an AI chatbot to Pages, Keynote, and Numbers\nEmma Roth Oct 27\nData center backlash is uniting America\nLauren Feiner Oct 27\nAdvertiser Content From\nThis is the title for the native ad\nTop Stories"
